cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the associated paper."
type: software
title: "HalluGuard: registry-aware Chain-of-Verification (CoV-RAG) middleware for validating Python package dependencies in LLM-generated code"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/massenon/HalluGuard"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and replication package for HalluGuard, a middleware
  prototype that validates third-party Python dependencies in LLM-generated code
  before installation via a short-circuiting chain of existence, security-posture
  and contextual-relevance checks. Note that the record-level evaluation files in
  data/ are reconstructed from reported aggregates rather than raw experimental
  logs; see data/PROVENANCE.md.
keywords:
  - package hallucination
  - slopsquatting
  - chain-of-verification
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - software supply-chain security
